  "term": "spastic paraplegia",
  "definition": "Spastic paraplegia, especially the familial form, refers to a varied group of disorders mainly marked by gradually increasing stiffness and weakness in the legs. The familial type has been linked to many different genetic locations and patterns of inheritance.",
